    "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nFixes two XPU-only failures in `test_attention_sink_deepseek_hy_loading_uses_parameter_loader` seen in [Buildkite intel-ci build 14222](https://buildkite.com/vllm/intel-ci/builds/14222#01a13cd3-6a2e-4f68-90bb-bf8575cef5c1). Follow-up to #57797, which added this test.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `torch.cuda.Event` shim (`_xpu_event`) was a plain function, not a class. `_torch_cuda_wrapper` patches it onto `torch.cuda.Event` permanently (by design), so any later `torch.cuda.Event | None` annotation evaluated in the same process (e.g. in `deepseek_v41/common/engram.py`) raised `TypeError`, since only types support `|`. Fixed by making `_xpu_event` a class, matching the existing `_EventPlaceholder` pattern in `vllm/v1/worker/cpu/shm.py`.\n- `hy_v4` legitimately doesn't support XPU (`vllm/models/hy_v4/__init__.py` raises `NotImplementedError` on import). The test parametrization didn't skip it on XPU, so it failed outright. Added `skipif(current_platform.is_xpu())`, following the existing ROCm-only `skipif` pattern already used in this file.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/worker/test_xpu_model_runner.py tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_reload.py -k \"torch_cuda_wrapper or attention_sink_deepseek_hy\" -v\n```\nAll pass (hy_v4 cases skip, since this sandbox itself resolves to the XPU platform). Also reproduced the original `TypeError` against the pre-fix code and confirmed it's gone after the fix. `ruff check` passes.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>**",
